Open in github.dev Open in a new github.dev tab Open in codespace Name Name Last commit message Last commit date fix(coding-agent): respect agentDir for sdk session paths #2457 6c8ac01 · 3,319 Commits.github.github chore: approve contributor zmberber .husky.husky fix(ai,coding-agent): make pi-ai browser-safe and move OAuth runtime … .pi.pi chore: add wrap-it prompt template packages packages fix(coding-agent): respect agentDir for sdk session paths #2457 scripts scripts fix(coding-agent,ai): restore Bun binary lazy provider loading #… .gitattributes.gitattributes chore: add repository.gitattributes for line ending normalization .gitignore.gitignore fix(coding-agent): normalize raw git URLs in extension source matching AGENTS.md AGENTS.md feat(ai): lazy-load provider modules for faster startup #2297 CONTRIBUTING.md CONTRIBUTING.md Fix Discord link LICENSE LICENSE Initial monorepo setup with npm workspaces and dual TypeScript config… pi.dev domain graciously donated by exe.dev Pi Monorepo Looking for the pi coding agent? See packages/coding-agent for installation and usage.Tools for building AI agents and managing LLM deployments.Packages Package Description @mariozechner/pi-ai Unified multi-provider LLM API (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.) @mariozechner/pi-agent-core Agent runtime with tool calling and state management @mariozechner/pi-coding-agent Interactive coding agent CLI @mariozechner/pi-mom Slack bot that delegates messages to the pi coding agent @mariozechner/pi-tui Terminal UI library with differential rendering @mariozechner/pi-web-ui Web components for AI chat interfaces @mariozechner/pi-pods CLI for managing vLLM deployments on GPU pods Contributing See CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution guidelines and AGENTS.md for project-specific rules (for both humans and agents).Development npm install # Install all dependencies
npm run build # Build all packages
npm run check # Lint, format, and type check
./test.sh # Run tests (skips LLM-dependent tests without API keys)
./pi-test.sh # Run pi from sources (must be run from repo root) Note:npm run check requires npm run build to be run first. The web-ui package uses tsc which needs compiled .d.ts files from dependencies.License MIT Releases
